{"repositoryId":271616776,"availability":"available","full":"twostraws/wwdc","name":"wwdc","description":"WWDC Community: Learning and sharing together","category":"Education","language":null,"stars":2180,"forks":217,"created":"2020-06-11T18:15:01Z","updated":"2026-06-26T18:11:43Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://wwdc.swiftgg.team/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:13.033Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:13.033Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:13.033Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:01:13.033Z","stars":2180,"forks":217}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The Apple development community is open and inclusive to everyone, and during WWDC we want to make sure everyone can join events, share articles about Apple’s new announcements, or just hang out with like-minded folks.","So, a number of us decided to start this repository to host links to various WWDC events, news, and tutorials from around the community. That means this repo will contain links to events being organized around our community, plus content from SwiftUI Lab, Hacking with Swift, Donny Wals, Swift with Majid, and many more – and we would love to share your articles too.","The Swift community is a thriving and exciting one, but it can sometimes feel a bit personality-driven. This repository was started to encourage everyone in our community to share their learnings, their perspectives, and their social events regardless of their background."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/twostraws/wwdc/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e5b9877211b0cf8567dd7dddddde9c9e504f18ab8e0d746a19e46f6871947832","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:13.167Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:13.167Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The Apple development community is open and inclusive to everyone, and during WWDC we want to make sure everyone can join events, share articles about Apple’